{
  "about": {
    "summary": "Canonical cross-language fixture for acton-service-client endpoint failover (crate 0.2.1). Every client that mirrors the failover behaviour (the Rust crate, and the TypeScript port in AxorumHQ/axorum) must reproduce every row. Consumers vendor a copy; this file is the source of truth.",
    "version": 1,
    "units": "Durations are whole milliseconds (_ms) or whole seconds (_s, Retry-After only).",
    "reason_shape": "A rotation reason / attempt outcome is {\"kind\":\"status\",\"status\":N} | {\"kind\":\"connect\"} | {\"kind\":\"timeout\"}.",
    "validation": "Endpoint 0 is the base URL; failover endpoints are numbered from 1. Each failover endpoint is checked in order: a bare http(s) origin (not_an_origin), then the base URL's scheme (mixed_scheme), then a new origin once normalized (duplicate_origin). The first failure is the error. Origins display as scheme://host:port with the default port filled in.",
    "scenarios": "Each scenario is a sequence of calls on one client, sharing its sticky preference. Each call lists every attempt in send order: the endpoint the client must choose, the scripted result, the time it takes (latency_ms, default 1; a stall takes the attempt timeout), and, for every attempt but a call's last, when the next attempt goes out ('now', or 'after' a pause). A virtual clock starts at 0 for each call; time advances only by attempt time and pauses. 'draws' (jitter 'full' scenarios only) feed the jitter draw, one per computed (non Retry-After) pause, in order; with jitter 'none' the draw is unused and no draws are listed. 'observed' is every call of the retry observer, in order: a rotation (the endpoint left and the reason) or a retry (the endpoint re-sent to, the reason, and the number of the attempt about to be sent, counted over the call). A 'reset' result is a transport failure after the request was written (a connection reset mid-body): neither connect nor timeout, so it is returned as it is ('reset' outcome) and never retried. 'outcome' is the call's result; for endpoints_exhausted, 'attempts' is the full trace and 'last' the final attempt's own error. For ok, 'attempts' is the trace the returned response carries: every attempt whose outcome asked for another try (a rotation or a retry), in send order, so empty when the first attempt answered, and ending with the returned response itself when the budget ran out on an accepted status that asks for another try. An endpoint whose results are 'connect' is refused on every attempt.",
    "decision_rules": [
      "Rotation outcomes: a status in retry_on_status (checked before accept_status), a connect failure, an attempt timeout. Other statuses retriable by default (429, 502, 503, 504; 423 only with Retry-After) and not accepted retry the SAME endpoint. Everything else ends the call.",
      "Nothing is retried unless a policy is set and the method is idempotent (GET, HEAD, DELETE, PUT) or the request is marked retriable.",
      "A rotation within a cycle is immediate. After n consecutive rotations (n = set size) the client pauses: the smallest Retry-After if every rotation in the cycle carried one, else pause(k, draw, remaining) with k = pauses taken so far + 1. A same-endpoint retry resets the cycle and pauses the same way (Retry-After, else pause(k, ...)).",
      "max_attempts counts sends: no further attempt once attempts_sent >= max_attempts. A pause that would reach the deadline is not taken.",
      "Before each send, if the deadline has passed: deadline_exceeded with attempts 0 when nothing was sent; otherwise the budget is spent.",
      "Budget spent (max_attempts, deadline, or refused pause): if at least one rotation was made (an attempt was actually sent to the next endpoint), endpoints_exhausted with the trace, unless the last outcome was an accepted status, which is returned as a success; otherwise the last outcome as it is.",
      "Sticky preference: any response whose status is not a rotation status for the request moves it to that endpoint; transport failures and rotation statuses never do. The next call starts there.",
      "The retry observer fires when a re-send is actually sent: a rotation when it goes to the next endpoint (with the endpoint left and the reason), a retry when it goes to the same endpoint (with that endpoint, the reason, and the attempt number). A single endpoint never rotates: every rotation outcome retries in place, exactly as 0.2.0, and is observed as a retry.",
      "Completeness: 'observed' has exactly one entry for every attempt but the last, in send order, with that attempt's endpoint ('left' for a rotation, 'endpoint' for a retry) and outcome as its reason; a retry's attempt number is the index of the attempt it re-sends plus two. The last attempt is never observed: its outcome is the call's outcome. Observer calls run synchronously on the caller's task."
    ]
  },
  "reasons": [
    { "reason": { "kind": "status", "status": 421 }, "label": "421", "proves_not_processed": true },
    { "reason": { "kind": "status", "status": 503 }, "label": "503", "proves_not_processed": false },
    { "reason": { "kind": "status", "status": 429 }, "label": "429", "proves_not_processed": false },
    { "reason": { "kind": "connect" }, "label": "connect", "proves_not_processed": true },
    { "reason": { "kind": "timeout" }, "label": "timeout", "proves_not_processed": false }
  ],
  "validation": [
    {
      "name": "clean_set_normalizes_in_order",
      "base": "https://A.example/api",
      "failover": ["https://b.example", "https://c.example:8443/"],
      "endpoints": ["https://a.example:443", "https://b.example:443", "https://c.example:8443"]
    },
    {
      "name": "single_endpoint",
      "base": "http://a.example:8080/gateway",
      "failover": [],
      "endpoints": ["http://a.example:8080"]
    },
    {
      "name": "duplicate_after_normalization",
      "base": "https://a.example",
      "failover": ["https://b.example", "HTTPS://A.EXAMPLE:443/"],
      "error": { "kind": "duplicate_origin", "origin": "https://a.example:443", "first": 0, "duplicate": 2 }
    },
    {
      "name": "duplicate_between_failovers",
      "base": "https://a.example",
      "failover": ["https://b.example:443", "https://B.example"],
      "error": { "kind": "duplicate_origin", "origin": "https://b.example:443", "first": 1, "duplicate": 2 }
    },
    {
      "name": "mixed_scheme",
      "base": "https://a.example",
      "failover": ["http://b.example"],
      "error": { "kind": "mixed_scheme", "index": 1, "expected": "https", "found": "http" }
    },
    {
      "name": "same_host_other_port_is_distinct",
      "base": "http://127.0.0.1:8080",
      "failover": ["http://127.0.0.1:8081"],
      "endpoints": ["http://127.0.0.1:8080", "http://127.0.0.1:8081"]
    },
    {
      "name": "path_refused",
      "base": "https://a.example",
      "failover": ["https://b.example/api"],
      "error": { "kind": "not_an_origin", "index": 1, "reason": "it has a path" }
    },
    {
      "name": "query_refused",
      "base": "https://a.example",
      "failover": ["https://b.example/?x=1"],
      "error": { "kind": "not_an_origin", "index": 1, "reason": "it has a query" }
    },
    {
      "name": "fragment_refused",
      "base": "https://a.example",
      "failover": ["https://b.example/#top"],
      "error": { "kind": "not_an_origin", "index": 1, "reason": "it has a fragment" }
    },
    {
      "name": "user_info_refused",
      "base": "https://a.example",
      "failover": ["https://user:pw@b.example"],
      "error": { "kind": "not_an_origin", "index": 1, "reason": "it carries user info" }
    },
    {
      "name": "other_scheme_refused",
      "base": "https://a.example",
      "failover": ["ftp://b.example"],
      "error": { "kind": "not_an_origin", "index": 1, "reason": "its scheme must be http or https" }
    },
    {
      "name": "not_a_url_refused",
      "base": "https://a.example",
      "failover": ["https://b.example", "not a url"],
      "error": { "kind": "not_an_origin", "index": 2, "reason": "it is not a valid absolute URL" }
    }
  ],
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "misdirected_then_next_succeeds",
      "about": "The addressed endpoint answers 421; the next one answers and becomes preferred.",
      "endpoints": 2,
      "policy": { "max_attempts": 4, "base_delay_ms": 100, "max_delay_ms": 1600, "jitter": "none", "deadline_ms": 15000 },
      "request": { "method": "POST", "retriable": true, "retry_on_status": [421, 503] },
      "calls": [
        {
          "preferred_before": 0,
          "attempts": [
            { "endpoint": 0, "result": { "kind": "status", "status": 421 }, "next": { "kind": "now" } },
            { "endpoint": 1, "result": { "kind": "status", "status": 200 } }
          ],
          "observed": [
            { "kind": "rotation", "left": 0, "reason": { "kind": "status", "status": 421 } }
          ],
          "outcome": {
            "kind": "ok",
            "status": 200,
            "attempts": [
              { "endpoint": 0, "outcome": { "kind": "status", "status": 421 }, "rotated": true }
            ]
          },
          "preferred_after": 1
        }
      ]
    },
